I've taken time off from nethack and started trying to ascend a knight.
It is getting more fun.  There were some things I wanted to do.

1. Twoweapon - I hadn't done it before.  I think I wanted the shield
for reflection or something when I was a barbarian, and then I played a
wizard.

2. spells - I wanted to be a fighter who also did spells.  When I
ditched my shield that helped.  Then I wished for a helm of brilliance.
I've been accumulating spell books.  The most fun is identify.  Even
though it fails 50 % of the time, it is still great.

3. riding a dragon.  I haven't done this yet, but I have a taming
scroll, saddle, and a black dragon waiting at the castle.

I'm thinking of doing a little more prep work - make some holy water,
bless things that need it. and then I'm going below the castle.

Also fun (kind of) was finding out how to waste a wish on an artifact.
I guess it is all part of learning.

Also, this time I didn't get dragon scale mail with a wish.  I made it
from white dragon scales.  That was pretty cool.

I haven't really done much jumping or jousting, but I might do it just
for fun.

Anyway, I'm not doing any conducts, but I'm trying to just have fun
with knight specific stuff and things I haven't done before.

